{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01142",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 5.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.65,
      "end_seconds": 11.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.24,
      "end_seconds": 18.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.09,
      "end_seconds": 28.85,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Honestly, um, it's loose stools after meals, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.86,
      "end_seconds": 41.91,
      "duration_seconds": 8.05,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.96,
      "end_seconds": 59.42,
      "duration_seconds": 15.46,
      "text": "Yes, coffee and stress. That makes it worse. About a five out of ten. Actually, and there's cramping lower tummy pain as well, five days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.65,
      "end_seconds": 63.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Nothing like blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.4,
      "end_seconds": 67.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "No, no blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.5,
      "end_seconds": 72.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Have you noticed weight loss or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.01,
      "end_seconds": 77.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.17,
      "end_seconds": 84.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.05,
      "end_seconds": 87.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "no, that's all normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.79,
      "end_seconds": 91.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.15,
      "end_seconds": 121.28,
      "duration_seconds": 25.13,
      "text": "I have anxiety, for five years i thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't it's the not knowing that gets to me oh, I have heart failure, for about ten years i told my wife I'd come today i have an irregular heartbeat"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.66,
      "end_seconds": 125.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Right, is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.44,
      "end_seconds": 132.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "yes, heart failure is known to us, good to have that clear what's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.02,
      "end_seconds": 138.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.42,
      "end_seconds": 141.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.5,
      "end_seconds": 147.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.71,
      "end_seconds": 150.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.19,
      "end_seconds": 155.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.07,
      "end_seconds": 176.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.31,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.96,
      "end_seconds": 191.55,
      "duration_seconds": 13.59,
      "text": "It's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. Spironolactone, 25 milligrams, once a day. Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 196.2,
      "end_seconds": 205.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "it's, It's meant to be twice a day, though I don't see he take it every time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.21,
      "end_seconds": 210.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "um, it's loperamide, 2 milligrams, when needed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.31,
      "end_seconds": 230.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.69,
      "end_seconds": 233.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "no, never"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.05,
      "end_seconds": 237.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.84,
      "end_seconds": 250.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.27,
      "end_seconds": 277.62,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "okay: pulse 82, temperature 36.9, pressure 116 over 71, oxygen saturation is 98 percent"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 278.59,
      "end_seconds": 280.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.68,
      "end_seconds": 284.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.36,
      "end_seconds": 291.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.43,
      "end_seconds": 296.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.64,
      "end_seconds": 311.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "your tummy is soft and only mildly tender on the left"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.35,
      "end_seconds": 326.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 330.69,
      "end_seconds": 344.02,
      "duration_seconds": 13.33,
      "text": "Good, you can sit up again. Let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with irritable bowel syndrome with diarrhoea at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.44,
      "end_seconds": 347.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Is it dangerous, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.28,
      "end_seconds": 364.07,
      "duration_seconds": 15.79,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with irritable bowel syndrome with diarrhoea do well once it's treated properly let me repeat that back to make sure you've had loose stools after meals, and no weight loss or fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.56,
      "end_seconds": 367.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.58,
      "end_seconds": 389.55,
      "duration_seconds": 20.97,
      "text": "I'm going to order a coeliac blood test, for diarrhoea. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm going to order a stool test, for diarrhoea. Keep a food diary and cut back on coffee."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.05,
      "end_seconds": 399.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.71,
      "text": "Sure. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. Let's review you in six weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.2,
      "end_seconds": 407.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 409.19,
      "end_seconds": 413.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "so, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.8,
      "end_seconds": 419.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "Mm, uh, no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}